{
  "name": "Weekly contractor insurance & bond expiration alerts -> Google Sheets + Slack (Apify)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Weekly contractor insurance & bond expiration alerts -> Google Sheets + Slack\n\n**What it does:** every Monday morning at 07:00 it runs the Apify Actor *Contractor License, Insurance & Bond Expiration Radar* (`RickyZ1X~contractor-license-insurance-bond-radar`) for Washington State (WA L&I), keeps active contractors whose general liability insurance policy, surety bond, or contractor license expires within the next 30 days, appends them to Google Sheets, and posts a weekly renewal outreach digest to Slack.\n\n### Setup (about 10 minutes)\n1. **Apify token**: Apify Console -> Settings -> API & Integrations -> copy your personal API token. In the *Run Apify Actor (expiration radar)* node create a **Header Auth** credential: Name = `Authorization`, Value = `Bearer YOUR_APIFY_API_TOKEN`.\n2. **Google Sheets**: create a sheet whose first row has these headers: `Contractor, Phone, License, Status, Alert Type, Earliest Expiry, Days Left, Insurer, Insurance Agency, Bond Surety, Bond Amount USD, City, Specialties`. Paste the spreadsheet ID into *Append to Google Sheet* and pick the tab.\n3. **Slack**: connect a Slack credential and set the channel (e.g. `#renewal-alerts`) in *Post Slack digest*.\n4. Click **Test workflow** once, then **Activate**.\n\n### Cost\nRuns are billed to *your* Apify account per event (`contractor-record`, plus `expiring-alert-record` for contractors with an active expiration alert inside your window). `maxRecords` in the JSON body caps the spend per run. The Apify free plan's monthly credit is enough to test it.\n\n### Compliance\nB2B use only. Data comes from official Washington State L&I public contractor registration records and contains **no consumer or homeowner data**; phone numbers are the contractor's registered business phone numbers. You are responsible for complying with the TCPA, the National Do-Not-Call Registry, state telemarketing laws, and insurance solicitation rules.",
        "height": 720,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "7b2e3a10-0001-4c1a-9b10-b0b0b0b00001",
